## enterprise-linux audit baseline -- project components (layer 13 + Control API)
## eld is the future control daemon (docs/CONTROL-API.md). Paths may not exist
## yet; watches on missing parents are ignored (-i in 10-el-base.rules).

## Policy and configuration written through the Control API
-w /etc/el/ -p wa -k el_config
## Device state, cached role mappings, hardening manifest
-w /var/lib/el/ -p wa -k el_state
## JIT elevation grants are rendered here by eld (PERMISSIONS.md §4)
-w /etc/sudoers.d/ -p wa -k el_jit_sudoers
## The daemon binary: replacement or execution outside systemd
-w /usr/libexec/eld -p wax -k el_eld_bin
-w /usr/bin/elctl -p wa -k el_eld_bin
## API socket directory (runtime; created by systemd RuntimeDirectory=eld)
-w /run/eld/ -p wa -k el_eld_socket
## Unit file and hardening drop-ins
-w /etc/systemd/system/eld.service.d/ -p wa -k el_eld_unit
-w /usr/lib/systemd/system/eld.service -p wa -k el_eld_unit
